  }
 },
 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:09:59.430533Z",
 "text": "No, this clause is not enforceable. \n\nUnder Ontario's *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006*, a fixed-term tenancy automatically renews as a month-to-month (or periodic) tenancy at the end of the term unless validly terminated under the Act. \n\nSpecifically, subsection 37(5) of the Act states that a notice of termination given by a tenant (or an agreement to terminate a tenancy) is **void** if it is given at the time the tenancy agreement is entered into, or as a condition of entering into the tenancy agreement. Because this clause requires the tenant to sign a notice of termination at the same time they enter into the lease (and none of the narrow exemptions such as student housing apply), both the contractual requirement and any resulting notice of termination are void and unenforceable.\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 37",
 "finish_reason": "STOP",
 "input_tokens": 191,
 "output_tokens": 1256,
